<title>USA: Lexmark elects three directors to new terms.</title>
<headline>Lexmark elects three directors to new terms.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Ky. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lexmark International Group Inc said Friday that William Fields, Stephen Hardis and Michael Maples were elected Friday to new terms on the board of directors at the corporation's annual meeting. Their terms will expire in the year 2000.</p>
<p>Fields, 47, is an advisor to the board of directors of Hudson's Bay Co who becomes president, chief executive officer and a director of Hudson Bay in June.</p>
<p>Hardis, 61, is chairman and CEO of Eaton Corp. Maples, 54, is the former executive vice president and a former member of the Office of the President of Microsoft Corp. Each had been serving a term which expired today.</p>
